# Kemetica — Node.js + MongoDB Backend: Models & Controllers

## Project Overview

**Kemetica** is a luxury Egyptian tour/expedition booking platform. The Angular frontend uses a clean **Domain-Driven Architecture** (domain → data → presentation layers) and currently calls mock data. The backend must replace those mocks with a real REST API at `/api/v1/`.

### Auth & Request Headers
The Angular [`apiInterceptor`](file:///d:/kemetica/src/app/core/interceptors/api.interceptor.ts) automatically attaches to every HTTP request:
- `Content-Type: application/json`
- `X-App-Client: Kemetica-Web`
- `withCredentials: true` — the JWT is stored in an **HttpOnly cookie** set by the backend, so the browser sends it automatically on every request. No manual `Authorization` header needed.

> **Security note:** HttpOnly cookies cannot be accessed by JavaScript — they are immune to XSS attacks. The backend must set `SameSite=Lax` (or `Strict`) and `Secure` (in production) on the cookie.

