### Angular Interceptor & App Config — cookie auth:
The [`apiInterceptor`](file:///d:/kemetica/src/app/core/interceptors/api.interceptor.ts) must be updated to set `withCredentials: true` so the browser includes the HttpOnly cookie on every cross-origin request. No manual header reading needed.

**Interceptor update needed:**
```ts
// core/interceptors/api.interceptor.ts
export const apiInterceptor: HttpInterceptorFn = (req, next) => {
  const modifiedReq = req.clone({
    withCredentials: true,           // ← sends HttpOnly cookie automatically
    setHeaders: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json',
      'X-App-Client': 'Kemetica-Web',
    },
  });
  return next(modifiedReq);
};
```

**Backend CORS must allow credentials:**
```js
// app.js
app.use(cors({
  origin: 'http://localhost:4200',   // Angular dev server
  credentials: true,                 // ← required for cookies
}));
```

**Backend JWT middleware reads from cookie:**
```js
// middleware/protect.js
const token = req.cookies.kmt_token;
if (!token) return res.status(401).json({ status: 'error', message: 'Not authenticated' });
const decoded = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET);
req.user = decoded;
```

**Extra npm package needed:** `cookie-parser`
```js
const cookieParser = require('cookie-parser');
app.use(cookieParser());
```

